@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] shared-first-screen-counts-belong-to-source
Native first-screen pull-request size hints MUST belong to the active source lease.
Changing server, account or Access authorization MUST revoke previous leases; a late
old writer or invalidator MUST NOT alter the current source's counts. Native memory
MUST remain bounded while the existing Android large-list behavior stays compatible.
Source: Tavi's accepted 21 Oct 2026 iOS source-isolation and maximum-reuse plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] shared-opening-counts-belong-to-native-source
Both hosts MUST populate first-frame pull-request sizes through a lease for their
current opaque endpoint/account/Access identity and invalidate it on source changes.
An invalidated or replaced lease MUST NOT read, refill or invalidate the current
source's sizes. Native memory MUST remain bounded while the existing Android
large-list behavior stays compatible. Unknown new list counts MUST remove an older
revision's counts. The existing Android put/get API MUST remain available. Source:
the accepted 21 Oct 2026 identity isolation plan and existing PullSizes first-frame
behavior (pr-opens-at-once).
